    <p class="font-extrabold text-[color:var(--color-ink)]"><a class="underline" href="https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/stress">NCCIH summary: diaphragmatic breathing</a></p>
    <p class="mt-1 text-[0.9375rem] leading-snug text-[color:var(--color-ink)]">A 2019 review of three studies with 880 participants found early evidence of better stress-related measures, including some cortisol results.</p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[0.9375rem] leading-snug text-[color:var(--color-ink-muted)]"><strong>For tracking:</strong> this is not a proven dose or a guaranteed hormone drop for one person.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[color:var(--color-border)] p-4">
    <p class="font-extrabold text-[color:var(--color-ink)]"><a class="underline" href="https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/stress">NCCIH summary: HRV biofeedback</a></p>
    <p class="mt-1 text-[0.9375rem] leading-snug text-[color:var(--color-ink)]">A review of 24 studies with 484 participants found benefits for stress and anxiety that people reported themselves.</p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[0.9375rem] leading-snug text-[color:var(--color-ink-muted)]"><strong>For tracking:</strong> biofeedback research doesn't prove an app's cortisol estimate. How you say you feel and a hormone test are different results.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[color:var(--color-border)] p-4">
    <p class="font-extrabold text-[color:var(--color-ink)]"><a class="underline" href="https://www.niddk.nih.gov/health-information/endocrine-diseases/cushings-syndrome">NIDDK: Cushing's syndrome</a></p>
    <p class="mt-1 text-[0.9375rem] leading-snug text-[color:var(--color-ink)]">Diagnosis and treatment deal with long-lasting excess cortisol and its cause.</p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[0.9375rem] leading-snug text-[color:var(--color-ink-muted)]"><strong>For tracking:</strong> general stress research can't replace a proper check of an abnormal hormone result.</p>
  </div>
</div>
<p><small>Sources checked September 17, 2026. The NCCIH page summarizes earlier research; these are not Cortisol+ trials. We have not measured an effect of Cortisol+ on laboratory cortisol.</small></p>

<h2>How long does it take to lower cortisol levels?</h2>
<p><strong>There is no set timeline.</strong></p>
<p>A short feeling of calm, a change in sleep and a medically meaningful hormone change are three different things.</p>
<p>If a doctor is monitoring your cortisol, ask them when it makes sense to check again. This guide doesn't promise normal levels in days, weeks or months.</p>

