<h2>When does high cortisol need medical treatment?</h2>
<p><strong>Long-lasting excess cortisol needs medical care, and treatment depends on the cause.</strong></p>
<p><a href="https://www.niddk.nih.gov/health-information/endocrine-diseases/cushings-syndrome">NIDDK explains that Cushing's syndrome involves long exposure to too much cortisol</a>. Treatment may mean changes to prescribed medicine or other medical care.</p>
<p><strong>Don't stop or cut back prescribed glucocorticoid (steroid) medicine yourself.</strong> Any change needs guidance from whoever prescribed it.</p>
<p>Symptoms that don't go away, or an abnormal test result, are worth discussing with a clinician. A wellness score can't confirm or rule out a hormone (endocrine) disorder.</p>
<p>Our <a href="/cortisol/test/">at-home testing guide</a> explains the difference between collecting a sample and interpreting it.</p>

<h2>How can I tell whether my routine is helping?</h2>
<p><strong>Track what you can actually see:</strong> sleep timing, how you feel, or wearable readings taken the same way each time. Keep these separate from any lab report.</p>
<p>Our <a href="/cortisol/track/#separate-records">guide to comparing lab results with wearable observations</a> gives you a simple way to do this.</p>
<p>Cortisol+ brings your available HRV, sleep and activity data into one view. Its <a href="/how-it-works/">published methodology</a> explains the wellness score and its limits.</p>
<p>It can't measure cortisol or prove that a treatment or lifestyle change worked. Analysis needs a subscription or an eligible trial.</p>

<ZenTip image="/app-ui/zen_new_low.webp">
  A plain notebook works fine. Jot down <strong>bedtime, wake time and one word for your mood</strong> each day.
</ZenTip>

<h2>Can I lower cortisol naturally without buying anything?</h2>
<p><strong>Yes, you can work on everyday stress habits for free.</strong> You don't need to buy a test, app or supplement.</p>
<p>Start with a routine you can keep up. Use a plain notebook if you want to track how it goes.</p>
<p>If you need a medical check, lifestyle tracking is useful background. It doesn't replace the check.</p>
